// Element is whatever a raw ADT hosts. The host requires no behavior of its guest:
// the guest owns its own identity and memory rules.
// Because it requires nothing, every type satisfies it; that is why it belongs only
// in the element and value positions of the raw ADT protocols.
// A domain protocol never takes or returns it: a domain concept that holds elements is its own
// type whose methods take and return the domain element type (docs/khayyam/polymorphism.md).
tp Container_Element ab

